A||N||6||gkozlov||Headlight conversion and headliner||||5||
Z||000000||gkozlov||06-27-2000||10:23 AM||||First I must apologize, I could seem to use the search function. I kniw both of these have been discussed.<BR> <BR>My 86 SE with sunroof has no headliner. The previous owner just glued carpet to the roof. I found a headliner at my local junkyard but it is broke  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/99102.gif"> <BR>Can this be repaired and how?<P>Second question. I want to chang over to the 87-88 type headlight motors. Has any one done this? How much of the headlight wiring harness must be changed over? Does any body have any for sale cheap?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jumpwing_1.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||06-27-2000||10:40 AM||||You can patch broken headliner board with polyester (fiberglass) resin.  Apply a patch of glass fabric across the wound, on  upper side of board.<P>Yes, you can convert to 1987-88 headlight system.  MI Fiero Club website has one of the better descriptions: <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/headlight.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/headlight.htm</A><BR>You'll have to scroll down almost to the bottom, where they discuss converting to the new system.  <P>As it happens, I was able to modify my 1986 headlight motors to work with a 1987+ Firebird headlight controller, so you don't HAVE to buy new motors.  BUT - if you can find the motors in salvage yard same time you obtain the controller, it's probably better, and definitely less work.<P>You'll have a MUCH easier time getting parts for the your new headlight system from 1987-up Firebird(s).   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 06-27-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-27-2000||01:11 PM||||StuGood--Why would you want to change everything over to the newer style headlight motor system <B>except</B> the motors?  That's the only reason I can thing of to change.  The newer motors are quieter and much (MUCH, <B>MUCH</B>) cheaper to rebuild.  Just curious, not flaming. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||06-27-2000||01:28 PM||||Because I'm cheap, and I already had the (old) motors there.  If I remember correctly, the new-style motors had already been pulled from the Firebird I got the controller from.<P>...plus, wanted to see if it would work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!! <P><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 06-27-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000004||BN Boomer||06-27-2000||04:08 PM||||Here's a repost of my response to a previous thread on swapping headlights.<P><BR>I recently did this same swap from my 87 Coupe parts car to my 85 GT. Yes, almost everything about this swap is simple nuts, bolts, and electrical plugs. I say "almost" because on the 87 there is a control module between the driver's side fender and firewall forward of the front wheel that is sort of a pain to get out. You'll need to at least remove the rivet and screws and pull back the fender and front fascia to get at the screws holding this module in place. When putting it into your 85, you'll have to decide whether to go to the pain of putting it back in there or relocating it somewhere inside the headlight compartment. Either way, you'll need to drill a couple of holes to install it. Also plan on removing the hoods, the A/C condensor mounting bolts, and at least loosening the radiator mounting bolts on both cars in order to fish the wiring wiring harness out intact from in front of the radiator of the 87 and then reinstalling it in the 85. It takes a bit of time to do, but isn't difficult and is better and looks cleaner than splicing wiring harnesses, in my opinion.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||gkozlov||06-27-2000||04:45 PM||||Thanks alot. I think Ill do it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||06-27-2000||06:11 PM||||Reminds me - in case you get your controller from a Firebird, it's mounted to a bracket on firewall near brake master cylinder.<P>The controller is a more-or-less flat black plastic thing with 2 connectors to it, with  raised letters that say "GUIDE".<P>Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !||||reg||3
